# Source-check ledger · 29 October 2026

All game wording is original paraphrase or an explicitly described teaching comparison. No source passage was copied into the game as an unattributed historical quotation. Creating an argument does not declare it true.

## Checked claims

- **Greek politics:** [Aristotle, Politics III](https://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/politics.3.three.html) supplies participation in judgment/office and common versus sectional advantage. The exclusion case is identified as Athens, not a universal definition of every polis. The question “who is included?” is our critical comparison, not an egalitarian position credited to Aristotle. [Plato, Republic VI](https://classics.mit.edu/Plato/republic.7.vi.html), especially 488–489, supplies the ship comparison and its relation to knowledge. This does not equate every modern expert with a philosopher-ruler.
- **Roman law:** [Institutes I.2–5](https://droitromain.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/Anglica/just1_Moyle.htm) supports simultaneous recognition of natural freedom, legal slavery and manumission. These legal categories are not flattened into “citizen/non-person”; individual freedom is not universal abolition. The compilation/editing comparison is a teaching contrast, not an asserted lineage from Alexandrian critical editing. [Berkeley’s Robbins manuscript exhibition](https://www.law.berkeley.edu/research/the-robbins-collection/exhibitions/medieval-law-school/) independently grounds the later Bologna glossing and circulation. Eastern Roman compilation → medieval Latin interpretation is documented; it is not confused with the separately preserved Greek/Syriac/Arabic/Latin philosophical translations.
- **Authority and consent:** [Hobbes, Leviathan XVII–XVIII and XXI](https://www.gutenberg.org/files/3207/3207-h/3207-h.htm) distinguishes subjects’ mutual authorization from a sovereign signing a contract, and connects obligation to protection. The sovereign can be an assembly, not necessarily a monarch. [Locke, Second Treatise §§95–99 and 221–222](https://www.gutenberg.org/files/7370/7370-h/7370-h.htm) grounds consenting association, majority action, trust and resistance. Neither case says that historical populations all actually consented, or that resistance automatically succeeds. The older fellowship/benefit cards are comparisons, not a claim of simple direct descent.
- **Haiti:** [The municipal abolition memorial’s chronology](https://memorial.nantes.fr/chronologie-des-abolitions/) distinguishes the 1791 uprising, local 1793 abolition and the national extension in 1794. The card’s range avoids pretending one uniform decree covered every locality at once. [The 1801 constitution](https://www.marxists.org/history/haiti/1801/constitution.htm), arts.1–5 and 14–16, explicitly combines French sovereignty and abolition with restrictions on agricultural workers’ movement. The optional prose does not need to repair this: both propositions appear in the tile labels. [The Haitian primary law collection at the Library of Congress](https://www.loc.gov/resource/gdcwdl.wdl_14719/?st=gallery) grounds actual local institutional production. [The 1804 declaration](https://declarationproject.org/?p=210) supports permanent separation; [BnF’s archival account](https://heritage.bnf.fr/france-ameriques/en/haitis-independence-debt-slave-unit-account-1794-1922) gives the distinction between 1804 independence and later coerced recognition. Enslaved people are actors, not passive recipients of European ideas. This is not a complete account of revolutionary factions, violence, gender, agricultural regimes or subsequent rulers.
- **Condensed science/art:** [National Gallery’s perspective entry](https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/glossary/perspective) supports the representational system; the frame/fixed-eye tile is an authored setup, not a claim that every historical painter used one apparatus. [Royal Museums Greenwich](https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/time/harrisons-clocks-longitude-problem) supports portable reference clocks and actual sea testing. [Einstein’s own teaching text, §§8–9](https://www.gutenberg.org/files/5001/5001-h/5001-h.htm) supports the train/embankment comparison. **Different reception order alone is insufficient**: equal train-midpoint distances and invariant light speed remain visibly separate before the simultaneity conclusion. No equation or hidden arithmetic is introduced.

## Access and uncertainty

The attempted Avalon law pages were unavailable to the web tool; they are not used as inspected evidence. A guessed former Brown exhibit address returned 404 and is not cited. Successful university-hosted primary texts and actual collections supplied alternatives. No denied/paywalled material was recovered or bypassed.

Some source translations are old or modern interpretive choices. The source-review stage checks the bounded distinctions above, not all translation controversies, every constitutional practice, or a definitive intellectual genealogy. Independent historical and forward-intuition review remains required. The preserved bibliography is broader than claims newly inspected here; old Atlas citations do not become fresh fact checks merely because they were cloned.

## In Our Time derivative use

Read existing `MINING-FINDINGS.md`, final redesign handoff and the metadata catalogue’s retention statement. These already explain the old Atlas’s breadth. The optional six new directions are short factual catalogue entries (dates, titles, programme links, provenance) only. They do not carry abstracts, transcripts, audio, inferred episode contents or invented listening claims. Catalogue attribution/licence accompanies the metadata; BBC content is not relicensed by it.
